<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico places $300 mln in dollar puts.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico places $300 mln in dollar puts.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed $300 million in dollar puts offered at an auction among banks on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank said it placed the puts at an average premium of 13.86 pesos per $1,000.  </p>
<p>The puts were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    *Maximum premium    20.00 pesos</p>
<p>    *Minimum premium    11.16 pesos</p>
<p>    *Average premium    13.86 pesos</p>
<p>    Initial date	  April 16, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity		April 30, 1997</p>
<p>    Participants	  12</p>
<p>    Assigned bids	  9</p>
<p>    Amount assigned	 $300 million</p>
<p>    Amount auctioned	$300 million</p>
<p>    Demand		 $1.530 bln</p>
<p>*Premium payable per $1,000</p>
<p>*Dollar put auction results may also be seen on fixed page MXAAS.</p>
<p>((--Adriana Valladares, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9593))</p>
</text>
